1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,289
A ball whirled on a string.

2
00:00:02,289 --> 00:00:04,025
A planet circling the Sun.

3
00:00:04,025 --> 00:00:05,432
A stone in a sling.

4
00:00:05,832 --> 00:00:07,698
All of them go around a point.

5
00:00:08,148 --> 00:00:10,946
Diya whirls a ball on
a string over her head.

6
00:00:10,946 --> 00:00:12,572
Its speed stays the same.

7
00:00:12,922 --> 00:00:17,473
But its direction changes every
moment, so its momentum keeps changing.

8
00:00:17,473 --> 00:00:19,420
Does anything stay the same?

9
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:20,820
Yes.

10
00:00:20,373 --> 00:00:21,457
Angular momentum.

11
00:00:21,457 --> 00:00:24,352
And even a ball in a
straight line can have it.

12
00:00:24,952 --> 00:00:27,797
Momentum, p, is mass times velocity.

13
00:00:28,147 --> 00:00:32,487
Angular momentum is its turning
version: how much a body goes around a

14
00:00:32,487 --> 00:00:33,387
point.

15
00:00:33,435 --> 00:00:34,779
We write it as L.

16
00:00:34,779 --> 00:00:39,130
It always needs a chosen point,
like the hand that holds the string.

17
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:41,206
It depends on three things.

18
00:00:41,206 --> 00:00:42,247
The momentum p.

19
00:00:42,247 --> 00:00:44,109
The distance r from the point.

20
00:00:44,109 --> 00:00:45,784
And the angle between them.

21
00:00:46,384 --> 00:00:48,515
Our motion notebook, from above.

22
00:00:48,515 --> 00:00:52,956
A half kilogram ball on a half metre
string, at two metres per second.

23
00:00:53,306 --> 00:00:57,047
The position vector r runs
from the hand to the ball.

24
00:00:57,047 --> 00:01:01,061
The momentum p is along the
path, at right angles to r.

25
00:01:01,461 --> 00:01:03,222
So L is r times p.

26
00:01:03,222 --> 00:01:05,378
Zero point five times one.

27
00:01:05,378 --> 00:01:06,812
Zero point five.

28
00:01:07,212 --> 00:01:10,447
On the graph, the x part
of p swings up and down.

29
00:01:10,447 --> 00:01:11,678
But L stays flat.

30
00:01:12,178 --> 00:01:15,964
Now a longer string, zero
point eight metres, same speed.

31
00:01:15,964 --> 00:01:17,915
L grows to zero point eight.

32
00:01:18,515 --> 00:01:19,487
Now you try.

33
00:01:19,487 --> 00:01:22,449
Diya halves the string,
but keeps L the same.

34
00:01:22,449 --> 00:01:24,827
Must the ball go slower, or faster?

35
00:01:24,827 --> 00:01:26,034
Pause and decide.

36
00:01:29,134 --> 00:01:30,034
Faster!

37
00:01:29,814 --> 00:01:30,946
L is m v r.

38
00:01:30,946 --> 00:01:33,128
Half the r needs twice the v.

39
00:01:33,778 --> 00:01:34,930
Now the surprise.

40
00:01:34,930 --> 00:01:37,664
A ball rolls in a
straight line, past Diya.

41
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:40,319
It moves at one metre per second.

42
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:43,489
Its line passes zero point
four metres from her.

43
00:01:43,889 --> 00:01:44,942
Slow-mo replay.

44
00:01:44,942 --> 00:01:45,842
Freeze.

45
00:01:45,941 --> 00:01:47,957
r and the angle keep changing.

46
00:01:47,957 --> 00:01:52,285
But the perpendicular from Diya to
the line is always zero point four.

47
00:01:52,685 --> 00:01:55,793
So L stays at zero point
two, the whole way.

48
00:01:55,793 --> 00:01:58,722
A straight line, and
still angular momentum.

49
00:01:59,322 --> 00:02:02,099
Let's build the formula,
one step at a time.

50
00:02:02,449 --> 00:02:03,349
Step one.

51
00:02:03,325 --> 00:02:05,464
Angular momentum is a vector.

52
00:02:05,464 --> 00:02:07,067
L equals r cross p.

53
00:02:07,817 --> 00:02:08,717
Step two.

54
00:02:08,611 --> 00:02:10,565
Its size is r p sine theta.

55
00:02:11,315 --> 00:02:12,275
Step three.

56
00:02:12,275 --> 00:02:16,677
r sine theta is the perpendicular
distance to the line of motion.

57
00:02:16,677 --> 00:02:19,045
So L is r perpendicular times p.

58
00:02:19,795 --> 00:02:20,730
Step four.

59
00:02:20,730 --> 00:02:23,543
In a circle, theta is ninety degrees.

60
00:02:23,543 --> 00:02:26,948
So L is m v r, which is m r squared omega.

61
00:02:27,698 --> 00:02:28,598
Step five.

62
00:02:28,463 --> 00:02:31,126
The unit is kilogram
metre squared per second.

63
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:34,437
Curl your right hand fingers from r to p.

64
00:02:34,437 --> 00:02:37,133
The thumb gives L, here out of the screen.

65
00:02:37,733 --> 00:02:38,812
Remember this.

66
00:02:38,812 --> 00:02:42,994
Angular momentum is momentum times
the perpendicular distance from the

67
00:02:42,994 --> 00:02:43,894
point.

68
00:02:44,309 --> 00:02:47,430
So why does the straight
ball have angular momentum?

69
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:50,701
L is measured about a point, not a path.

70
00:02:51,101 --> 00:02:54,342
The line misses Diya by
zero point four metres.

71
00:02:54,342 --> 00:02:56,572
So r perpendicular is not zero.

72
00:02:56,972 --> 00:03:00,068
And along a straight
line, it never changes.

73
00:03:00,068 --> 00:03:02,868
So L is not zero, and stays the same.

74
00:03:03,468 --> 00:03:04,423
Side by side.

75
00:03:04,423 --> 00:03:08,295
In a circle, r is fixed, and the
angle stays at ninety degrees.

76
00:03:08,695 --> 00:03:11,696
In a straight line, r
and the angle change.

77
00:03:11,696 --> 00:03:13,867
Only r perpendicular stays fixed.

78
00:03:14,467 --> 00:03:15,367
Your turn.

79
00:03:15,285 --> 00:03:19,682
Is there any point about which the
straight ball has no angular momentum?

80
00:03:19,682 --> 00:03:20,885
Pause and decide.

81
00:03:24,085 --> 00:03:26,498
Yes, any point on its own line!

82
00:03:26,498 --> 00:03:29,869
There, r perpendicular
is zero, so L is zero.

83
00:03:30,519 --> 00:03:32,209
Now, one worked example.

84
00:03:32,559 --> 00:03:37,740
A two kilogram particle at three i plus
four j metres moves at two i metres

85
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:38,741
per second.

86
00:03:38,741 --> 00:03:40,646
Find L about the origin.

87
00:03:41,146 --> 00:03:42,742
First, p is m v.

88
00:03:42,742 --> 00:03:45,284
Four i kilogram metres per second.

89
00:03:46,034 --> 00:03:47,502
L is r cross p.

90
00:03:47,502 --> 00:03:49,897
Three i cross four i is zero.

91
00:03:49,897 --> 00:03:52,992
Four j cross four i is minus sixteen k.

92
00:03:53,742 --> 00:03:56,206
Size sixteen, pointing into the screen.

93
00:03:56,956 --> 00:04:01,538
Check: it moves along y equals
four, so r perpendicular is four.

94
00:04:01,538 --> 00:04:03,468
Four times four, sixteen.

95
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:05,579
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:05,929 --> 00:04:10,240
Many students think a body moving in a
straight line has no angular momentum.

97
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:11,540
Not true.

98
00:04:11,493 --> 00:04:15,671
About any point off its line,
L is r perpendicular times p.

99
00:04:16,321 --> 00:04:18,026
Where is this asked?

100
00:04:18,026 --> 00:04:23,001
In L as r cross p, in m v r for
circles, and in projectiles.

101
00:04:23,601 --> 00:04:24,794
Exam level now.

102
00:04:24,794 --> 00:04:29,635
A zero point one kilogram ball is thrown
at twenty metres per second, thirty

103
00:04:29,635 --> 00:04:31,394
degrees above the ground.

104
00:04:31,394 --> 00:04:32,596
Take g as ten.

105
00:04:32,596 --> 00:04:37,266
Find its angular momentum about the
launch point, at the highest point.

106
00:04:42,666 --> 00:04:44,038
The answer is C.

107
00:04:44,038 --> 00:04:45,346
Five root three.

108
00:04:45,846 --> 00:04:50,317
At the top, the velocity is horizontal:
twenty cos thirty, or ten root

109
00:04:50,317 --> 00:04:51,217
three.

110
00:04:51,406 --> 00:04:55,072
The height is u squared sine
squared theta over two g.

111
00:04:55,072 --> 00:04:56,057
Five metres.

112
00:04:56,557 --> 00:04:58,806
That height is the moment arm.

113
00:04:58,806 --> 00:05:00,202
So L is m v h.

114
00:05:00,202 --> 00:05:03,550
Zero point one times ten
root three times five.

115
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:05,691
Here is your recap.

116
00:05:05,691 --> 00:05:07,275
Screenshot this card.

117
00:05:10,475 --> 00:05:12,413
Can you answer these without help?

118
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:13,713
One.

119
00:05:13,268 --> 00:05:16,942
How can a ball moving in a straight
line have angular momentum?

120
00:05:17,842 --> 00:05:18,742
Two.

121
00:05:18,269 --> 00:05:20,038
About which points is it zero?

122
00:05:20,938 --> 00:05:21,838
Three.

123
00:05:21,461 --> 00:05:24,409
Why is L equal to m v r
for a ball on a string?

124
00:05:25,309 --> 00:05:29,725
Next time: push a merry-go-round
for longer, and it spins faster.

125
00:05:29,725 --> 00:05:30,625
Why?
